    "title": "How to Maintain Competitive Balance with Revenue Sharing in College Sports, SEC Commissioner Says It's \"A Real Threat\" - NewsBreak",
    "text": "It’s a whole new world in college sports with many new rules starting this month. Universities are now able to pay athletes directly, and they raise money from their communities, which raises questions about how to maintain competitive balance when some communities may be able to afford more resources than others. SEC Commissioner Greg Sankey says this is “a real threat” that requires proper guardrails and accountability for member institutions. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WJTV.",
